course: dictionary
lesson: 11751
title: Ballast: the weight that keeps things steady
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ballast is heavy material put low down in something to keep it steady. It can be stones, sand or water. Ships, submarines and balloons all use it.
explain: «The sailors filled the empty ship with sand as ballast.» Sand is heavy and sits low, so the ship does not tip over in the waves. Ask yourself: what would keep the ship steady? Ballast fits that job.
explain: «The hot-air balloon dropped a sandbag to rise higher.» Less ballast means less weight, so the balloon floats up. Ballast can also mean steadiness in life, as in «Her calm nature was ballast for the team.»
fact: Ballast means heavy material put low down to keep something steady.
fact: Ships, submarines and hot-air balloons all use ballast.
fact: Submarines take in water as ballast to sink, and pump it out to rise again.
fact: Railway workers lay stone ballast under the tracks to hold them in place.
fact: «Ballast» can also mean something that gives steadiness or balance to a person or plan.
exercise: «The ship carried heavy sand low in its hold as ballast.» What is the ballast for? | To make the ship go faster | To hold up the sails | To paint the ship | *To keep the ship steady
exercise: «The hot-air balloon dropped a sandbag so it could rise.» Why did it drop ballast? | It was too cold to fly | It wanted to make a loud noise | It was going to sink into the sea | *It became lighter and floated higher
exercise: Workers laid stones under the railway track to hold it in place. What is this stone called? | *Ballast | Ballot | Ballad | Balcony
test: «The submarine took in water as ballast so it could sink.» What does ballast mean here? | *Heavy material that helps control how deep it goes | Warm air | A kind of engine | A small fish that lives in the sea
test: «Her calm nature was ballast for the whole team.» What does ballast mean here? | A loud noise | *Something that gives steadiness | A type of ship | Heavy sand in a bag
exam: What is the main job of ballast? | *To keep something steady and balanced | To make a boat float away | To make things heavier and slower | To make a loud noise
